{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgNFm7RVUw2Tzmyib3Mcs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The correction is done and verified. `outputs/greeting.txt` now contains exactly `Hello, Ada.` followed by one newline, written through the single declared native Writer effect under the authorized grant. Nothing else in the workspace changed.\n\n**Basis verified before work.** The pinned cut `stdo://releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/` is installed and valid with zero failures, and its manifest hash equals the pin in fixture_product.json. All seven installed skill files hash exactly to the receipt. I routed through the stdo-workspace-change and stdo-tool-operations skills and used the configured stdo_ac MCP tools, which TOOLING.md declares equivalent to the CLI.\n\n**What the tool route recorded.** Every operation returned status ok with no refusal.\n\n| Step | Request id | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| Read name | greeting-fix-read-name-1 | content `Ada` + newline |\n| Read output preimage | greeting-fix-read-greeting-pre-1 | content `Hello, Grace.` + newline |\n| Read requirement, design, control TASK.md | greeting-fix-read-requirement-1, -design-1, -control-task-1 | acquired, evidence retained |\n| Observe output parent | greeting-fix-observe-outputs-prewrite-1 | artifact 6b308af4… passed to the write |\n| Write | greeting-fix-write-greeting-1 | effect completed, end established |\n| Re-observe vs baseline | greeting-fix-observe-postwrite-1 | diff lists only outputs/greeting.txt |\n\n| Target hash | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Preimage | dbfa3fcacaedf5e16d125ee1410774c6cb2d0bbd0a9fb07cacfe87fd362d29c7 |\n| Postimage, reported by the tool | 8b1560f395c0248eca4d2d6cc361825a9f8c00d11ce6f52b26eea2872573c2c1 |\n| Postimage, computed independently from the file | 8b1560f395c0248eca4d2d6cc361825a9f8c00d11ce6f52b26eea2872573c2c1 |\n| Expected hash of `Hello, Ada.` plus one newline | 8b1560f395c0248eca4d2d6cc361825a9f8c00d11ce6f52b26eea2872573c2c1 |\n\n**Preservation.** A hash snapshot of all 26 workspace files before and after differs on the one target line only. Both host configurations, the Claude receipt, every installed skill file, the Codex config, and the unrelated sentinel are byte-identical. No package update or removal, Git action, network call, new actor, ticket, or global configuration occurred. Two scratch hash lists were written to /tmp outside the workspace for the diff and then removed.\n\n**Closure, stated with the correct predicates.**\n- **Candidate available:** the exact corrected bytes exist at the target with retained preimage, postimage, and effect evidence.\n- **Not performed, by design:** semantic acceptance and independent review. Every tool response limits itself to output availability, GOALS.md says no acceptance or publication is inferred, and no review was required inside this fixture. Owner assessment of the result remains open to the qualification executive.\n\n**One limit on my reading.** The tools.describe response exceeded the tool output cap and was saved to a file. I read its status, operation names, unsupported list, builder, method profile, and the full contracts for source.read, workspace.observe, and work.write. I did not read the other 19 operation schemas or the refusal code table, as none were needed here."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8883,"cache_read_input_tokens":84522,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8883},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"77c68056-c6c9-483e-9faa-2ab2c7d7322a","uuid":"d87ca36b-c07f-419d-9f22-07547b4b862b","timestamp":"2026-10-25T03:36:38.102Z","request_id":"req_011CgNFm72fu4mK1eutd6P6q"}
